  m_Name: Debrief_M1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: LastSignal.Core::LastSignal.DebriefCard
  title: Why mass is the enemy of every mission
  concept: 'Newton''s second law: acceleration = thrust / mass'
  nasaSource: 'NASA Glenn Research Center, Beginner''s Guide to Rockets (Newton''s
    laws of motion) [person 6: confirm exact page]'
  body: The same engine pushes a heavier frame more slowly. Every kilogram you add
    needs more thrust, and on a real rocket more propellant, which is more mass again
    (the rocket equation). Engineers fight for every kilogram. Part masses and thrusts
    in M1 are game-balance values.
